// Five equal bars, 3:2.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Aromantic Pride Flag"
  designer "Cameron Whimsy"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2014-11"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20230319173943/https://cameronwhimsy.tumblr.com/post/102698477928/whoops-yeah-i-just-realised-i-never-actually-made"
  source "https://crwflags.com/FoTW/FLAGS/qq-arom.html"
  source "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aromantic_Pride_Flag.svg"
  note "Designer's own post, read from the Wayback snapshot above, dated 16 Nov 2014. The designer says it was written for this version of the flag after the fact. It names five bars (green and light green for the aro spectrum, white for platonic, grey and black for the sexuality spectrum) but states no proportion or hex values."
  note "This is the November 2014 redesign. An earlier version by the same designer, published 7 February 2014 per FOTW, had a yellow bar where this has white. FOTW also records an older four-bar green, yellow, orange and black flag of unknown origin. Neither earlier flag is written here."
  note "Colors were sampled from the flag image in the designer's post (the 360 by 240 PNG, one value per bar): #3da642, #a8d379, #ffffff, #a9a9a9, #000000. The Commons drawing has #3da542 and #a7d379 for the greens, one step off."
  note "The proportion is the post's image's, 360 by 240, exactly 3:2. The designer states none in words. The Commons drawing, which Wikipedia's infobox shows, is 3:5."
}
palette {
  green "#3da642"
  light-green "#a8d379"
  white "#ffffff"
  grey "#a9a9a9"
  black "#000000"
}
proportion hoist=10 fly=15

bars green light-green white grey black
